## Why This Is Asked
This question introduces per-device ordering with cross-device parallelism in a realistic IoT setting and a simple degradation policy (coalescing). It tests concrete concurrency primitives (buffers, bounded queues, workers) and practical edge cases (backpressure, shutdown).

## Key Concepts
- Per-device FIFO buffers
- Bounded global queue
- Backpressure and degradation strategy
- Coalescing policy and determinism
- End-to-end test plan for ordering, degradation, and shutdown

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo sketch: coalesce to last N readings per device when backlog hits threshold
class DeviceBuffer {
  constructor(id) { this.id = id; this.queue = []; }
  push(reading) { this.queue.push(reading); }
  drain(n) { return this.queue.splice(0, n); }
}
```

